WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
So what does the code add?

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:06.550
One module, two scripts that only read, and
a single separate script that can write.

3
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.825
What drives it is a handful of small
files, each with a clear keeper.

4
00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:16.092
Identity engineering owns the reviewed
policy file and the rotation settings,

5
00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:19.125
like how early to raise
and how long to overlap.

6
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:22.012
Application owners keep
three simple records:

7
00:00:22.012 --> 00:00:26.232
which vault holds each app's
certificate, who approved each rotation,

8
00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:29.637
and who confirmed the workload
signs in with the new one.

9
00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:33.890
Every rotation carries one
request ID from start to finish.
